          cultural: 'Often played on hand-crafted wooden boards passed down through generations. A staple of inter-generational family gaming, church socials, and community gatherings, particularly in the upper Midwest (Minnesota, Wisconsin) and Canada.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        setup: {
          players: '2 to 6 players (can be played in teams with partners sitting opposite each other on a square board).',
          deck: 'Each player (or team) has their own full 52-card deck PLUS 2 Jokers (54 cards total per player deck). Keep decks separated by player.',
          equipment: '1. **Fast Track Board**: Hexagonal or square board with 64-68 spaces around the perimeter plus 4 Home Base centers (one per player/team). 2. **Marbles or Pegs**: 4 marbles per player in their color. 3. **Holding Pen**: Off-board area where marbles start before being entered into play.',
          dealing: 'Each player shuffles their own deck and draws 5 cards into their starting hand. Place remaining cards face-down as draw pile.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first player or team to move all 4 marbles from the Holding Pen around the board and into your Home Base (center area).',
          gameplay: "1. **Turn Sequence**: On your turn, play one card from your hand to move a marble. Draw one card from your deck to return to 5-card hand (unless the card says 'Play Again'). 2. **Exiting the Pen**: You can only move a marble OUT of the Holding Pen with specific 'Start' cards (Joker, Ace, King, Queen, Jack, or 6). These cards can also move your marble forward that many spaces. 3. **Forward Movement**: Play a card matching its number value. Face cards (K, Q, J) can move 10 spaces or exit the Pen. 4. **Backwards Movement (4s)**: The 4 is unique: play a 4 to move a marble BACKWARD 4 spaces. This is a powerful defensive move. 5. **Split Movement (7s)**: Play a 7 to move a single marble 7 spaces OR split the 7 between two different marbles (e.g., 3+4 or 2+5). 6. **Joker (Trump Card)**: Move a marble to any opponent's exact position (bumping them back to their Holding Pen) OR use as a Start card. Play Again. 7. **Play Again Cards**: Aces, 6s, Face Cards, and Jokers grant an extra turn (draw card, take another turn). 8. **Landing on Fast Track**: If you land exactly on a Fast Track entry space, you may use the central shortcut on your next turn to jump across the board.",
          keyRules: [
            "**Bumping**: If you land exactly on a space occupied by an opponent's marble, that opponent's marble returns to their Holding Pen.",
            "**Fast Track Shortcut**: A dangerous shortcut across the board's center. Easy bumping target but saves many spaces.",
            '**Blocking**: You cannot pass your own marbles. If a marble blocks your path, choose a different marble to move.',
            '**Must Move**: If you have a legal move, you MUST take it, even if disadvantageous.',
            '**Card Values**: 2-10 move forward that many spaces. J, Q, K = 10 spaces or Start. Ace = 1 space or Start. 6 = 6 spaces or Start and Play Again. 4 = Move backward 4 spaces. 7 = Move 7 spaces or split between two marbles. Joker = Trump (bump opponent or Start) + Play Again.',
            '**Home Base Entry**: Only certain positions allow entry into Home Base; marbles must enter from the correct position on the track.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize getting all 4 marbles out of the Holding Pen early. Start cards are your most valuable resource. Spread your marbles around the board to reduce risk of multiple bumps.',
          intermediate: "The Backwards 4 Trick: Use the 4 to move a marble backward into a 'shortcut' position that's only 4-6 spaces from Home Base entry. This converts a long board loop into a quick finish. **Fast Track Risk**: Avoid lingering on Fast Track spaces. Enter only if you can exit immediately.",
          advanced: "Team Coordination (Partnership Play): Sacrifice your own position to bump an opponent threatening your partner's marble. Use split 7s to advance your partner's marbles if rules allow. **Marble Positioning**: Position marbles to block opponents who are ahead. A strategically placed marble forces opponents into 3+ consecutive turns with bad cards.",
          tips: [
            "Always hold one 'Start' card if you have marbles remaining in the Holding Pen.",
            "Never stay on Fast Track longer than one turnâ€”you're a sitting duck.",
            "If you're far behind, use 4s aggressively to reset opponent positions.",
            'In the endgame with 1-2 marbles left, use face cards conservatively. Save Jokers for critical bumps.',
            "Track opponent hand sizes (do they have cards left to draw ). If an opponent is about to draw their last card, they're vulnerable to being forced into dead turns.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
